    <text xml:space="preserve">
        <body>
            
            <div type="edition" xml:lang="tam-Latn" rendition="class:vaṭṭeḻuttu maturity:83215">
                
                <p>
                    <lb n="1"/>kō-vicaiya-nantīccuva
                    <lb n="2" break="no"/>ra-vi<choice><sic>r</sic><corr>k</corr></choice>kirama-parumaṟku yāṇṭu nārpat
                    <lb n="3" break="no"/>tu nā<choice><sic>ṟ</sic><corr>ṉ</corr></choice>k-āvatu
                </p>
                <p>
                    malāṭṭu mēr-kōvalūr-nā
                    <lb n="4" break="no"/>ṭṭu Irāmantaivāṭi mēṟ maṅkaḷa-peru
                    <lb n="5" break="no"/>m<choice><orig>a</orig><reg>ā</reg></choice>ṉār paṭai vanta ñāṉṟu vāṇa-perumāṉārkk-ā
                    <lb n="6" break="no"/>y-p paṭṭāṉ vēṇar
                    <lb n="7" break="no"/>-k-kaḷiyaṉ			
                </p>
                
            </div>
            
            <div type="translation" resp="part:emfr">
                
                <p n="1-3">
                    Fourty-fourth <supplied reason="subaudible">year</supplied> of the victorious king Nantīccuvaravikkiramaparumaṉ.<note>Sanskrit Nandīśvaravikramavarman.</note>
                </p>
                <p n="3-7">
                    Vēṇarkkaḷiyaṉ fell for the sake of <supplied reason="explanation"><foreign>āy</foreign></supplied><!--Check translation!--> the Bāṇa lord when the army <supplied reason="subaudible">of</supplied> the lord of Maṅkalam marched<supplied reason="explanation"><foreign>vanta</foreign> <note>Literally: came.</note></supplied> upon Iṟamantaivāṭi in Mērkōvalūrnāṭu in Malāṭu.
                </p>
                
            </div>
            
            <div type="commentary"/>
            
